course: dictionary
lesson: 9635
title: Stumble: trip, mistake, or find by chance
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Stumble» has more than one meaning, so the words around it tell you which one the writer wants. Read the sentence first and ask what is happening.
explain: The first meaning is about walking or running: to trip and almost fall. «The explorer stumbled in the dark and grabbed a branch.» The dark and the grabbing tell you he nearly fell.
explain: The second meaning is about talking or reading: to make a mistake or get stuck. «She began to stumble over a hard word.» She is reading aloud, so stumble means getting stuck. The third meaning is to find something by chance: «The twins stumbled upon a secret cave.» Nobody was looking for it.
fact: Stumble can be a verb or a noun: you can stumble, or you can have a stumble.
fact: To stumble on, upon or across something means to find it by chance.
fact: «Stumble over» can mean getting stuck on a word when you read aloud.
fact: To stumble is to trip and almost fall when you are walking or running.
fact: In adventure stories, «stumbled upon a secret cave» shows a discovery nobody planned.
exercise: «The explorer stumbled in the dark and grabbed a branch.» What does stumbled mean here? | To find something by chance | To make a mistake in speaking | *To trip and almost fall | To shout loudly
exercise: «She began to stumble over a hard word when reading aloud.» What does stumble mean here? | To fall fast asleep | To run very fast | To find a coin | *To get stuck or make a mistake
exercise: «The twins stumbled upon a secret cave.» What does stumbled upon mean? | To break a window | To look very hard for something | To hide from someone | *To find something by chance
test: Safety notices say, «Clear the floor so nobody stumbles over toys or cables.» Why? | *To stop people tripping over things | To find lost toys | To make the floor shiny | To let the cables move freely
test: In «He made one stumble on the stairs, but he did not fall», what kind of word is stumble? | An adjective, describing the stairs | *A noun, naming a thing that happened | A verb, showing an action | A question word
exam: The shy boy began to stumble through his speech. What does stumble mean here? | To find his way by chance | To fall asleep on the stage | *To make mistakes or get stuck while speaking | To run away very fast
